  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "To His Father, When He Had Entrusted to Him the Care of the Church of Nazianzus.",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.2.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.2.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "ThisOration was delivered a.d. 372. Two years earlier Valens had divided Cappadocia into two provinces.",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.2.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.2.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Anthimus, Bishop of Tyana, asserting that the ecclesiastical provinces were regulated by those of the empire,",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.2.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.2.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "claimed metropolitical rights over the churches of Cappadocia Secunda, in opposition to S. Basil, who had hitherto been metropolitan of the undivided province.",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.2.s4",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.2.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "S. Basil, with the intention of vindicating the permanence of his former rights, created a new see at Sasima, on the borders of the two provinces, and with great difficulty prevailed upon S. Gregory to receive consecration as its first Bishop.",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.2.s5",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.2.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "S. Gregory, who had “bent his neck, but not his will,” was for a long time reluctant to enter upon his Episcopal duties,",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.2.s6",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.2.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and at last was prevailed upon by S. Gregory of Nyssa, S. Basil’s brother, to make an attempt to do so. When, however,",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.2.s7",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.2.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "he found that Anthimus was prepared to bar his entrance by force of arms, he returned home, definitely resigned his see, and once more betook himself to the life of solitude which he so dearly loved.",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.2.s8",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.2.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Recalled hence, he consented, at his father’s earnest entreaty, to undertake provisionally the duties of Bishop-coadjutor of Nazianzus: and pronounced this short discourse on the occasion of his installation.",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.3.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.3.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "1. I opened my mouth, and drew in the Spirit, and I give myself and my all to the Spirit, my action and speech, my inaction and silence,",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.3.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.3.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "only let Him hold me and guide me, and move both hand and mind and tongue whither it is right, and He wills: and restrain them as it is right and expedient.",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.3.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.3.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "I am an instrument of God, a rational instrument, an instrument tuned and struck by that skilful artist, the Spirit. Yesterday His work in me was silence.",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.3.s4",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.3.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "I mused on abstinence from speech. Does He strike upon my mind today? My speech shall be heard, and I will muse on utterance.",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.3.s5",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.3.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "I am neither so talkative, as to desire to speak, when He is bent on silence; nor so reserved and ignorant as to set a watch before my lips when it is the time to speak:",
    "chunk_index": 14,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.3.s6",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.3.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "but I open and close my door at the will of that Mind and Word and Spirit, Who is One kindred Deity.",
    "chunk_index": 15,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.4.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.4.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "2. I will speak then, since I am so bidden.",
    "chunk_index": 16,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.4.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.4.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And I will speak both to the good shepherd here, and to you, his holy flock, as I think is best both for me to speak, and for you to hear to-day.",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.4.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.4.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Why is it that you have begged for one to share your shepherd’s toil?",
    "chunk_index": 18,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.4.s4",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.4.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For my speech shall begin with you, O dear and honoured head, worthy of that of Aaron, down which runs that spiritual and priestly ointment upon his beard and clothing.",
    "chunk_index": 19,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.4.s5",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.4.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Why is it that, while yet able to stablish and guide many, and actually guiding them in the power of the Spirit, you support yourself with a staff and prop in your spiritual works?",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.4.s6",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.4.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Is it because you have heard and know that even with the illustrious Aaron were anointed Eleazar and Ithamar, the sons of Aaron?",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.4.s7",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.4.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For I pass over Nadab and Abihu, lest the allusion be ill-omened: and Moses during his lifetime appoints Joshua in his stead, as lawgiver and general over those who were pressing on to the land of promise?",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.4.s8",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.4.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The office of Aaron and Hur, supporting the hands of Moses on the mount where Amalek was warred down by the Cross, prefigured and typified long before, I feel willing to pass by, as not very suitable or applicable to us:",
    "chunk_index": 23,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.4.s9",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.4.s9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "for Moses did not choose them to share his work as lawgiver, but as helpers in his prayer and supports for the weariness of his hands.",
    "chunk_index": 24,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.5.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.5.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "3. What is it then that ails you? What is your weakness? Is it physical?",
    "chunk_index": 25,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.5.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.5.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "I am ready to sustain you, yea I have sustained, and been sustained, like Jacob of old, by your fatherly blessings. Is it spiritual?",
    "chunk_index": 26,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.5.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.5.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Who is stronger, and more fervent, especially now, when the powers of the flesh are ebbing and fading, like so many barriers which interfere with, and dim the brilliancy of a light?",
    "chunk_index": 27,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.5.s4",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.5.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For these powers are wont, for the most part, to wage war upon and oppose one another, while the body’s health is purchased by the sickness of the soul, and the soul flourishes and looks upward when pleasures are stilled and fade away along with the body.",
    "chunk_index": 28,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.5.s5",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.5.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But, wonderful as your simplicity and nobility have seemed to me before, how is it that you have no fear, especially in times like these,",
    "chunk_index": 29,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.5.s6",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.5.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "that your spirit will be considered a pretext, and that most men will suppose, in spite of our spiritual professions, that we are undertaking this from carnal motives.",
    "chunk_index": 30,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.5.s7",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.5.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For most men have made the office to be looked upon as great and princely, and accompanied with considerable enjoyment, even though a man have the charge and rule over a more slender flock than this, and one which affords more troubles than pleasures.",
    "chunk_index": 31,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.5.s8",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.5.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Thus far of your simplicity, or parental preference, if it be so, which makes you neither admit yourself, nor readily suspect in others anything disgraceful;",
    "chunk_index": 32,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 372,
    "date_range": [
      371,
      373
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12#GregNaz.Or12.5.s9",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-12",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or12.5.s9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "for a mind hardly roused to evil, is slow to suspect evil. My second duty is briefly to address this people of yours, or now even of mine.",
    "chunk_index": 33,
    "context_before": null,
